(7140403, 1093347, 102278, '<td valign="top">Oh, and regarding my initial comment about the photograph having a bit of a Leica feel to it, i''ve been looking at a lot of portraits by Alfred Weidinger recently who does remarkable things with a Leica and the 50mm 0.95 (and 75mm) and your portrait reminded me a bit of them. <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/a-weidinger/with/8330808184/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Check him out, i''m sure you''ll enjoy them.</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-12-08 07:30:10.</i></td>', 'Oh, and regarding my initial comment about the photograph having a bit of a Leica feel to it, i''ve been looking at a lot of portraits by Alfred Weidinger recently who does remarkable things with a Leica and the 50mm 0.95 (and 75mm) and your portrait reminded me a bit of them. Check him out, i''m sure you''ll enjoy them.', '2013-12-08 07:25:59.000000', '2013-12-08 07:30:10.000000', 0),
